  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n4 chairs + 14 tables = ₹4000\n\n16 chairs + 12 tables = ₹5000\n\nCalculation:\n\nLet 1 chair = x and 1 table = y\n\n4x + 14y = 4000 ⇒ Multiply (1) by 4 ⇒ 16x + 56y = 16000 ...(1) \n\n16x + 12y = 5000 ...(2)\n\n⇒ Subtract (2) from (1) ⇒ (16x + 56y) − (16x + 12y) = 16000 − 5000\n\n⇒ 44y = 11000\n\n⇒ y = 250\n\n⇒ From (1): 4x + 14 × 250 = 4\n000\n\n⇒ 4x + 3500 = 4000\n\n⇒ 4x = 500\n\n⇒ x = 125\n\n⇒ 8 chairs + 4 tables = 8 × 125 + 4 × 250\n\n⇒ 1000 + 1000 = 2000\n\n**∴ The cost of 8 chairs and 4 tables is ₹2000.**\n\n8b:T6",
